✅ 𝐀𝐧𝐬𝐢𝐛𝐥𝐞 𝐈𝐧𝐭𝐞𝐫𝐯𝐢𝐞𝐰 𝐒𝐜𝐞𝐧𝐚𝐫𝐢𝐨 #7 – 𝐑𝐮𝐧 𝐀𝐧𝐬𝐢𝐛𝐥𝐞 𝐑𝐨𝐥𝐞𝐬 𝐂𝐨𝐧𝐝𝐢𝐭𝐢𝐨𝐧𝐚𝐥𝐥𝐲

🧠 𝐐𝐮𝐞𝐬𝐭𝐢𝐨𝐧:

How do you include an Ansible role only if a 𝒄𝒐𝒏𝒅𝒊𝒕𝒊𝒐𝒏 𝒐𝒓 𝒇𝒍𝒂𝒈 𝒊𝒔 𝒕𝒓𝒖𝒆?

💡 𝐑𝐞𝐚𝐥-𝐖𝐨𝐫𝐥𝐝 𝐔𝐬𝐞 𝐂𝐚𝐬𝐞:

Imagine you're managing a multi-tier infrastructure.
Sometimes, a host should have Nginx, but sometimes it shouldn't — depending on 𝒆𝒏𝒗𝒊𝒓𝒐𝒏𝒎𝒆𝒏𝒕, 𝒉𝒐𝒔𝒕 𝒈𝒓𝒐𝒖𝒑, 𝒐𝒓 𝒂 𝒄𝒖𝒔𝒕𝒐𝒎 𝒇𝒍𝒂𝒈.

Hardcoding it into every playbook? That’s not scalable.

This is where conditional role execution becomes powerful.

🧠 𝐓𝐡𝐢𝐧𝐤 𝐨𝐟 𝐢𝐭 𝐥𝐢𝐤𝐞 𝐭𝐡𝐢𝐬:

You don’t install air conditioning in every room — just where it’s needed. ❄️

🔧 𝐒𝐨𝐥𝐮𝐭𝐢𝐨𝐧: 

Use when with roles in your playbook

You can use a variable like 𝒆𝒏𝒂𝒃𝒍𝒆_𝒏𝒈𝒊𝒏𝒙 to control whether a role gets applied.

💡 𝐏𝐫𝐨 𝐓𝐢𝐩𝐬:

✅ Set default values in 𝒅𝒆𝒇𝒂𝒖𝒍𝒕𝒔/𝒎𝒂𝒊𝒏.𝒚𝒎𝒍 within the role to avoid undefined variable errors.
✅ You can control roles per host, group, or environment by setting flags in 𝒊𝒏𝒗𝒆𝒏𝒕𝒐𝒓𝒚 𝒇𝒊𝒍𝒆𝒔 𝒐𝒓 𝒈𝒓𝒐𝒖𝒑_𝒗𝒂𝒓𝒔.

📦 Example: Include nginx role only when enabled

🎯 This way, you keep your playbooks 𝒎𝒐𝒅𝒖𝒍𝒂𝒓, 𝒄𝒍𝒆𝒂𝒏, 𝒂𝒏𝒅 𝒆𝒏𝒗𝒊𝒓𝒐𝒏𝒎𝒆𝒏𝒕-𝒂𝒘𝒂𝒓𝒆.

------

! run-role-conditionally.yaml 

name: Scenario #7 - Conditional Role Execution
hosts: webservers
become: yes
vars:
  enable_nginx: true
roles:
  - role: nginx
when: enable_nginx

